          "english_quote": "than that, later, unwillingly, you should perish in those very sins.",
          "issue": "The draft gives ἐφ’ ἁμαρτίαις a circumstantial sense, 'in those very sins.' A circumstantial use of ἐπί with the dative is defensible, but the natural causal alternative, 'because of those very sins,' materially changes how the sins relate to perishing. That alternative and the reason for choosing the circumstantial reading are absent from the notes. This is an interpretive disclosure problem, not evidence of source corruption.",
